b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays (5.2), procedures (5.4), the for statement with step-until and while elements (4.6) and conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each comparison as posed, to be tested on the values of x, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: F f1 ... fF, the number of facts of pick and then the value of each fact, in order. A line 2: c, the integer of x greater than c. Stage 3, which withdraws the relation of stage 2, has no constants;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P10d. One unknown x. Stage 1: pick(x), a closed world of facts. Stage 2: x greater than c2. Stage 3: withdraw the relation of stage 2. pick is given by its facts, which the program holds as given: when it is posed each fact, in order, gives x a value. Each comparison is held as posed by a Boolean that says whether it is in force. After every stage the values of x are those of the facts that pass every comparison in force, tested again from the facts. A withdrawal sets its comparison out of force. The comparison stays in the text, and nothing is restated;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, j, nf, c2, alive, tested;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ picked, r2, w2;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ xv[1:1000], pk[1:1000];
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ xa[1:1000];

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ test;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every value of x that pick gives is tested by every comparison in force, in the order the comparisons were posed. A comparison is held until pick has given x its values;
  i̲f̲ picked t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      xa[j] := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
      i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ tested := tested + 1; i̲f̲ ¬(xv[j] > c2) t̲h̲e̲n̲ xa[j] := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ test;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ digits(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a natural number, its decimal digits with no sign and no spaces, for the name of a case;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ digits(v ÷ 10);
    d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
    i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
  e̲n̲d̲ digits;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  picked := r2 := w2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; nf := 0; tested := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, and then that stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ pick(x): each fact, in order, gives x one value;
      nf := read;
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ xv[j] := read; pk[j] := 1 e̲n̲d̲;
      picked := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c2 := read; r2 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ withdraw the relation of stage 2;
      r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; w2 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;

    test;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answers: every value of x, or, before pick, x and the comparisons held;
    alive := 0;
    i̲f̲ picked t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ xa[j] t̲h̲e̲n̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
          alive := alive + 1;
          PRINTTEXT(`[answer]x = '); print(xv[j]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
        e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]x');
      i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held, where x gt '); print(c2) e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free');
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the values of x held, all at once, the comparisons in force and withdrawn, and the facts of pick applied;
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ picked ∧ alive = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ picked t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`values of x held, all at once:');
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ xa[j] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` '); print(xv[j]) e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
      NLCR;
      PRINTTEXT(`[problem-alternatives x '); print(alive); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`comparisons in force: ');
    i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x gt '); print(c2) e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`none');
    NLCR;
    i̲f̲ w2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`withdrawn: x gt '); print(c2); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ r2 ∧ ¬picked t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations 1]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[operations pick/'); digits(j); PRINTTEXT(` '); print(pk[j]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations x-gt-tested '); print(tested); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
